tryCatch: Error Handling in R
tryCatch() allows you to handle errors and other conditions gracefully:

tryCatch(
  {
    # Code to try
    result = risky_operation()
  },
  error = function(e) {
    # Handle errors
    print(paste("Error occurred:", e$message))
  },
  warning = function(w) {
    # Handle warnings
